Z||000000||mrfixit58||08-16-2001||01:06 PM||||I just received the latest Kit Car Magazine today. I couldn't help but chuckle when I ran across the title, "NORTHSTAR MR2" in the Kit Tech section. The anonymous writer states: " I have seen countless articles featuring Northstar V-8 swaps for Fieros. However, I have yet to see a swap performed on the similarly setup MR2.... ". He goes on to ask if for advice. The really humorous part is the response. The magazine's author basically says to take the back half of a Fiero and a welder and go to it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Too funny. <P>On a little side note... a picture of Phil's SC3800 88 Formula are shown as part of their coverage of the Hot Rod power Tour.<P>Just sharing, <P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||12
